 ‚¤textÙ The chief of all their strength.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse$…¤book§chapteri«first_verse%ªlast_verse+¦verses—„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0He brought them forth also with silver and gold:¦layout ‚¤textÙ7And there was not one feeble person among their tribes.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"Egypt was glad when they departed:¦layout ‚¤textÙ$For the fear of them fell upon them.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!He spread a cloud for a covering;¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And fire to give light in the night.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(The people asked, and he brought quails,¦layout ‚¤textÙ,And satisfied them with the bread of heaven.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.He opened the rock, and the waters gushed out;¦layout ‚¤textÙ(They ran in the dry places like a river.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#For he remembered his holy promise,¦layout ‚¤text¸And Abraham his servant.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ)And he brought forth his people with joy,¦layout ‚¤text½And his chosen with gladness:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse+…¤book§chapteri«first_verse,ªlast_verse-¦verses’„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'And gave them the lands of the heathen:¦layout ‚¤textÙ,And they inherited the labour of the people;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%That they might observe his statutes,¦layout ‚¤textÙ&And keep his laws. Praise ye the LORD.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse-